course: dictionary
lesson: 11467
title: Adversary: the one you compete against
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An adversary is someone you fight or compete against. It is a more formal word for an enemy or opponent. Stories are full of them. «The brave knight faced his adversary at the castle gate.»
explain: Look at the words around adversary to work out its meaning. The knight is facing someone at a gate, and they are about to fight. So an adversary is the person on the other side, not a friend on the same side.
explain: In games and sport, an adversary is the player or team you play against. «In the chess final, Maya met a worthy adversary.» Worthy tells you the adversary was strong, so Maya had to play her very best.
explain: Adversary can also mean a rival in public life. «The two political adversaries shook hands after the debate.» Even though they argued, they were still respectful. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "shook hands with their opponents" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: An adversary is someone you fight or compete against.
fact: Adversary is a noun. Its plural is adversaries.
fact: Adversary is a formal word, so you will often see it in stories, history and news.
fact: «A worthy adversary» means a strong opponent who makes you try harder.
fact: «Old adversary» means someone you have faced before, often in a long rivalry.
exercise: «The brave knight faced his adversary at the gate.» What is an adversary? | A castle wall | *A person you fight or compete against | A horse that carries a knight | A friend who helps you
exercise: «In the chess final, Maya met a worthy adversary.» What does a worthy adversary mean? | A coach who gives tips | A helpful team mate | A referee who stops the game | *A strong opponent
exercise: «The two political adversaries shook hands after the debate.» Find and copy the word that means people who oppose each other. | shook | debate | *adversaries | hands
test: «Our team's adversary was the team from the next town.» Who is the adversary here? | *The team we play against | Our coach | The new team kit | The referee
test: What is the plural of adversary? | adversarie | *adversaries | adversarys | adversary's
exam: «The knight and his adversary bowed before the fight began.» What is an adversary? | A kind teacher | A sword | *An enemy or opponent | A friend who cheers
